ouse cells (Knauf U et al. 1996; Kline MP & Morimoto RI 1997).<br>HSF1-ERK association was shown to promote ERK activity in human HeLa, acute monocytic leukemia THP1  and metastatic cutaneous SCC7 cells resulting in phosphorylation of HSF1 on Ser307 (Chu B et al. 1996; Wang X et al. 2004). This phosphorylation in turn promoted HSF1 association with YWHAE (14-3-3 epsilon), which may be involved in the attenuation of HSF1 activity during recovery and leads to accelerated cytoplasmic localization of HSF1 (Wang X et al. 2003, 2004). <br><br><br><br> ", "literatureReference": [4793878, 4793873, 4793902, {"dbId": 5096367, "displayName": "Sequential phosphorylation by mitogen-activated protein kinase and glycogen synthase kinase 3 represses transcriptional activation by heat shock factor-1", "title": "Sequential phosphorylation by mitogen-activated protein kinase and glycogen synthase kinase 3 represses transcriptional activation by heat shock factor-1", "journal": "J. Biol. Chem.", "pages": "30847-57", "pubMedIdentifier": 8940068, "volume": 271, "year": 1996, "url": "http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/8940068", "className": "LiteratureReference", "schemaClass": "LiteratureReference"}, {"dbId": 5083663, "displayName": "Repression of the heat shock factor 1 transcriptional activation domain is modulated by constitutive phosphorylation", "title": "Repression of the heat shock factor 1 transcriptional activation domain is modulated by constitutive phosphorylation", "journal": "Mol. Cell. Biol.", "pages": "2107-15", "pubMedIdentifier": 9121459, "volume": 17, "year": 1997, "url": "http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/9121459", "className": "LiteratureReference", "schemaClass": "LiteratureReference"}], "className": "Summation", "schemaClass": "Summation"}], "reviewStatus": {"dbId": 9821382, "displayName": "five stars", "definition": "externally reviewed", "name": ["five stars"], "className": "ReviewStatus", "schemaClass": "ReviewStatus"}, "isChimeric": false, "category": "transiti